cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lcc in research, please cite it as below."
title: "lcc: Local Context Compiler"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Local Context Compiler contributors"
version: "1.4.0"
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lucasmartins-ai/lcc"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/local-context-compiler/"
abstract: >-
  lcc removes old tool output from a coding agent's context. In its stashed mode, every byte
  it removes is one recall away, checked by hash, and each pass reports what it removed and
  why. It runs locally and offline by default, and its tool-call mode leaves every user and
  assistant message byte for byte.
keywords:
  - context compaction
  - coding agents
  - LLM context window
  - prompt caching
  - Model Context Protocol
